{
  "technical_and_design_decisions": [
    "U1: All AddXXX and UpdateXXX functions on ConfigTx are renamed to SetXXX with overwrite semantics; map-based values are unconditionally replaced; slice-based values (e.g., SetAnchorPeer) replace an existing matching entry instead of appending a duplicate; all call sites, tests, examples, and GoDoc are updated.",
    "U2: ConfigTx.Base() is renamed to BaseConfig() and ConfigTx.Updated() is renamed to UpdatedConfig(), with GoDoc and tests updated accordingly.",
    "U3: A chainable API is introduced via lightweight Go wrapper types (e.g., Channel, Application, Orderer, Org) that wrap the underlying *cb.ConfigGroup protos; ConfigTx exposes Channel(), Application(), Orderer() entry points, and each wrapper exposes its own getters/setters/removers (e.g., c.Application().Org(\"Org1\").SetAnchorPeer(...)); wrappers hold references to the same underlying proto tree so updates are applied in place.",
    "U4: A new configtx/orderer subpackage is created containing the orderer-related types (Kafka, EtcdRaft, BatchSize, ConsensusState, and related structs); only type definitions are moved, functions remain in configtx and are updated to reference the new package; package-level GoDoc is written.",
    "U5: A new configtx/membership subpackage is created containing MSP-related types (MSP, SigningIdentityInfo, OUIdentifier, CryptoConfig, NodeOUs, and related structs); functions remain in configtx and reference the new package; package-level GoDoc is written.",
    "U6: RemoveXXX functions are changed to return no error when the target value does not exist; where no other failure mode exists, the error return is removed from the signature entirely; callers, tests, and GoDoc are updated.",
    "U7: GoDoc is overhauled: trivial call-demonstration examples removed, Example_XXX functions renamed to describe their scenario, monolithic examples split into focused examples (ACLs, policy retrieval, orderer update, membership), '// Output:' validation blocks removed, and long lines wrapped so generated GoDoc has no horizontal scrolling; verified locally via 'godoc -http=:2020'.",
    "U8: A standalone demo CLI (configtx) is built as a separate module/package using a subcommand-style Go CLI framework (e.g., cobra); it supports generating system channel genesis blocks, application channel create transactions, and config update transactions for all updatable properties (anchor peers, ACLs, policies, MSPs, capabilities, orderer settings, consortiums) via flags/subcommands, reading/writing protobuf files; help text and a README document usage.",
    "All changes are implemented in Go using the existing protobuf definitions (common/config, policy, msp protos) with no changes to the proto schemas themselves; unit tests use the existing table-driven test style and golden-file comparison of marshaled configs."
  ],
  "assumptions": [
    "The starting codebase is the existing Hyperledger Fabric configtx (pkg/config) library with its current Add/Remove/Update functions, tests, and examples already in place.",
    "A single developer performs all work; effort is reported in person-hours of work, not elapsed time.",
    "The developer is proficient in Go, protocol buffers, and Hyperledger Fabric channel configuration concepts; no training ramp-up is included beyond initial codebase familiarization.",
    "Estimates include implementation, unit test updates/creation, GoDoc/example updates, and developer self-testing; external community code-review cycles are assumed lightweight with rework covered by the integration/refinement activity.",
    "U8 is a demo/sample CLI: it must be functional and well documented, but production-grade hardening (extensive input fuzzing, packaging/release pipelines, cross-platform distribution) is out of scope.",
    "No changes to fabric protobuf definitions or to peer/orderer binaries are required; integration of the library into other Fabric components is out of scope.",
    "The CLI reads and writes standard Fabric config protobuf files and reuses the configtx library; cryptographic signing of config updates by the CLI is limited to what the library already supports.",
    "Existing continuous integration (build, vet, lint, unit tests) is reused; only minor build configuration updates for the new packages and CLI module are needed."
  ],
  "activities": [
    {
      "activity_id": "1",
      "activity_name": "Codebase familiarization, design, and planning",
      "activity_description": "Review the existing configtx library structure, proto usage, tests, and examples; design the SetXXX semantics, chainable wrapper types, orderer/membership subpackage layout, and CLI command structure; set up development environment and verify baseline build/tests.",
      "most_likely_effort": 8
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "2",
      "activity_name": "U1 - Implement SetXXX functions with override semantics",
      "activity_description": "Rename all AddXXX/UpdateXXX functions to SetXXX; change add semantics to unconditionally overwrite existing values; implement duplicate-safe replacement for slice-based values such as SetAnchorPeer; update call sites, unit tests, examples, and GoDoc to reflect overwrite behavior.",
      "most_likely_effort": 24
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "3",
      "activity_name": "U2 - Rename Base()/Updated() accessors",
      "activity_description": "Rename ConfigTx.Base() to BaseConfig() and ConfigTx.Updated() to UpdatedConfig(); update GoDoc, tests, and examples referencing the old names.",
      "most_likely_effort": 4
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "4",
      "activity_name": "U3 - Chainable API with intermediate wrapper types",
      "activity_description": "Design and implement Channel/Application/Orderer/Org wrapper types around ConfigGroup protos; expose entry points on ConfigTx; implement getters, setters, and removers on each wrapper so calls can be chained (e.g., c.Application().Org(name).SetAnchorPeer()); refactor ConfigTx-level functions to delegate to wrappers; update examples, GoDoc, and unit tests.",
      "most_likely_effort": 64
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "5",
      "activity_name": "U4 - Create orderer subpackage",
      "activity_description": "Create configtx/orderer package; move Kafka, EtcdRaft, BatchSize, ConsensusState and related orderer types into it; update all references in configtx functions and tests; write package-level GoDoc.",
      "most_likely_effort": 8
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "6",
      "activity_name": "U5 - Create membership subpackage",
      "activity_description": "Create configtx/membership package; move MSP-related types (SigningIdentityInfo, OUIdentifier, CryptoConfig, NodeOUs, and associated MSP structs) into it; update all references in configtx functions and tests; write package-level GoDoc.",
      "most_likely_effort": 8
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "7",
      "activity_name": "U6 - Idempotent Remove functions",
      "activity_description": "Change all RemoveXXX functions so removing a non-existent value is a no-op without error; drop the error return where no other failure mode remains; update callers, unit tests, and GoDoc to document the behavior.",
      "most_likely_effort": 8
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "8",
      "activity_name": "U7 - GoDoc and examples overhaul",
      "activity_description": "Remove the seven listed trivial examples; improve documentation for configtx.New(); rename Example_XXX functions to scenario-based names; split large examples into focused ones (ACLs, policy retrieval, orderer update, membership); remove '// Output:' validation blocks; wrap long lines to avoid horizontal scrolling; verify rendered output with a local godoc server.",
      "most_likely_effort": 16
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "9",
      "activity_name": "U8 - Demo configtx CLI",
      "activity_description": "Implement a standalone CLI with subcommands and flags to generate system channel genesis blocks, application channel create transactions, and config update transactions for all updatable properties (anchor peers, ACLs, policies, MSPs, capabilities, orderer batch size/consensus settings, consortiums); read/write config protobuf files; implement help text and README usage documentation; add CLI-level tests.",
      "most_likely_effort": 80
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "10",
      "activity_name": "Cross-cutting unit test updates and coverage",
      "activity_description": "Update and extend the existing unit test suite across all renamed/moved/refactored APIs and new packages to maintain coverage, including table-driven tests and golden protobuf comparisons.",
      "most_likely_effort": 16
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "11",
      "activity_name": "Integration testing, regression, and bug fixing",
      "activity_description": "Run full library and CLI test suites; perform end-to-end verification of generated genesis blocks, channel creation transactions, and config updates; run vet/lint/CI builds; fix defects and address review feedback.",
      "most_likely_effort": 16
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "12",
      "activity_name": "Final documentation pass and release preparation",
      "activity_description": "Final review of all GoDoc, package docs, and CLI help/README for consistency and completeness; ensure examples compile and render correctly; finalize build configuration for new packages and CLI module.",
      "most_likely_effort": 8
    }
  ],
  "reported_total": {
    "most_likely_effort": 260
  }
}
